21:- Face names on the main board: the UNDER face carries all parts and faces the block floor; the TOP face is bare and faces the screen (`design/ecad/ring/pcb/board-notes.md:53`, `design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:6`).
55:| Main board `main_board` | PCB1 | 27.2 x 12.6 x 0.3 mm, 4 copper layers with laser microvias, parts on the under face only | `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:22`, `design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:6` | 1 |
96:- **Join:** every board part of `design/bom.csv` to the under face of PCB1, with solder paste and one reflow. The parts: U1 (`main_chip`), U2 (`power_chip`, nPM1304, `design/architecture.md:566`), R71, R72, U3 (`storage`), U10, U4 (`screen_supply_chip`), U5 (`mic_1`) and U6 (`mic_2`), Knowles SPK0641HT4H-1 (`design/architecture.md:654`, `design/bom.csv:9`), J1 (`screen_connector`), ANT1 (`antenna`, on the board's under face at X -10.80, Y 5.25, on its maker's land pattern, no notch), C89 (not fitted: the pad only) and LT1 (0 ohm) at the antenna (`design/bom.csv:85`, `design/bom.csv:86`), L2, L3, L4, C3, C12, X1 (`crystal_32M`), X2 (`crystal_32k`), L1, FB1, R1, R2, C1, C2, C5, C4, C6, C7, C10, C14, C11, L10 (`screen_supply_coil`), C21, C26, C27, C24, C25, C23, C22, C28, C29, C31, C32, C35, C36, R31, R32, R57, R58, R60, C60, U11 (`motor_regulator`, TLV75530PDQNR, at X 0.0, Y 4.2), C83 (`motor_cap_in`, X 0.0, Y 5.45), C84 (`motor_cap_out`, X 1.27, Y 5.0, turned 90) (`design/architecture.md:705`, `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:19` to `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:21`; the places are the model's proposal until the board layout confirms them, `design/architecture.md:760`), U9, R61 and R62 (now on U11's enable pin, `design/architecture.md:705`), R66, R63, R64, R65, C61, C72, C80, C81, C82, C71, C73, C74, C75, C78, C79, C76, C77, C85, C86, C87, C88 (`design/bom.csv:67` to `design/bom.csv:69`), L71 (`power_coil_1`), L72 (`power_coil_2`). The motor switch and the motor diode of earlier versions are not fitted: they left the design (`design/architecture.md:705`). LED1, R41 and Q2 are removed in v7 and are not fitted (`design/architecture.md:834`). The 15 test pads (TP1, TP3, TP4, TP5, TP6, TP8, TP9, TP11, TP12, TP14, TP15, TP17, TP18, TP19, TP21; TP2, TP7, TP10, TP13, TP16, TP20 and TP22 are dropped) and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B are copper on the same face and get no paste [PROPOSED: reason, a solder bump on a test pad or a hot-bar land spoils the spring-pin contact and the hot-bar joint of step 16]. C13 is not mounted (`design/bom.csv:18`).
120:- **Join:** nothing is joined. A jig touches the under face. SWD: TP3 SWDCLK, TP4 SWDIO, TP5 NRESET, TP17 VDD_1V8, TP18 GND; log: TP1 DBG_TX, send-only (the receive pad DBG_RX, TP2, is dropped) (`design/ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:44`, `design/architecture.md:291`). Power: the jig feeds a battery voltage on the J_BAND_B cell lands and a 10 k resistor on its thermistor land [PROPOSED: reason, the cell is not yet on the board and the power chip needs a battery and a thermistor reading], and VBUS, D-, D+, GND on the J_BAND_B pad lands, which are the USB lines of the four charging pads (`design/bom.csv:77`).
124:- **After:** this is the last moment the SWD pads can be reached. They lie on the under face, which faces the block floor 0.05 mm away once the board is in the body (`design/architecture.md:426`). After step 17 the only way into the chip is USB through the charging pads; a broken boot loader after step 17 means a scrapped ring (conflict K-A1).
201:- **Join:** FOAM1 (`foam`) on the board's top face; DISP1 (`screen`) on the foam; the screen's tail (`screen_tail`) folded round the board's hand end into J1 on the under face, latch closed (`design/mech/thin/placement.csv:25`, `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:18`).
